    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/human-resources-assistant-benefits-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Human Resources Assistant - Benefits",
      "description": "Human Resources Assistant - Benefits - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Human Resources Assistant - Benefits San Diego, California Full-time temporary 5704 Position Title & Department: Human Resources Assistant - Benefits; Human Resources Posting # 5704 Department Description: The role of Human Resources is to attract, retain and support a quality workforce so that collectively we can provide an exceptional educational experience for our students. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: This is a full-time temporary, benefit-based position. The appointment is renewable at the discretion of the University and dependent upon performance and continued funding. Under the direction of the Benefit Manager, reviews and approves benefit and insurance enrollments and changes for processing.  Reconciles and pays benefit and insurance premiums to the appropriate vendors. Provides administrative support for leave of absence and Workers’ Compensation claims.   Assists with annual open enrollment, new employee benefit orientations and monitors enrollment results.  Performs a broad spectrum of tasks in support of the Benefits department. Acts as the primary contact for first-level benefits inquiries for a variety of benefits programs including health and welfare, retirement, leave of absence, time off, PPACA and leave of absence. Works with highly confidential employee information and is responsible for compliance with privacy regulations under multiple state and federal regulations, including but not limited to: ERISA, COBRA, GINA, HIPPA, FMLA, CFRA, PDL, FEHA, the ADA and ADAAA, and FERPA, and supports programs and processes under the purview of the IRS, DOL, the Civil Rights Department and other local, state and federal jurisdictions. Duties and Responsibilities: Processes employee insurance and benefit enrollments and changes. Processes, files, and supports management of workers’ compensation claims. Responds to employee benefit inquiries timely. Assists with annual open enrollment and monitors enrollment results. Reconciles monthly vendor statements and troubleshoots and resolves discrepancies. May assists with administration of tuition exchange and tuition remission programs. Communicates with benefit vendors to resolve enrollment and service issues. Provides support to the benefits team in administration of employee retirement plans including answering questions and assisting employees with enrollment and plan contribution changes. Assists with scheduling various benefit-related events. Assists with the development and distribution of benefit educational materials. Assists with benefits communications including presentations to employees. Provide administrative support with employee leaves of absence. Assist in maintaining employee benefits files. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. High School Diploma or GED equivalent Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED equivalent 2+ years of general office experience required. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in related field preferred. Some general HR experience or experience in benefits highly preferred. Bilingual in Spanish highly preferred. Performance Expectations - Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Working knowledge of computers, MS Office and MS Outlook Working knowledge of the use of standard office equipment Exceptional customer service skills Excellent oral and written communication skills Detail-orientated Excellent telephone and virtual meeting etiquette Accurate typing and proofreading skills Basic spreadsheet skills (Excel, Sheets, or similar) Handle sensitive and confidential employment and payroll information with tact and discretion To relate effectively with a wide variety of people, both virtually and in-person Provide service in a courteous, prompt and efficient manner Cooperate as a team member with other Benefit team members, as well as the entire HR department Efficiently work in an ever-changing multi-task, multi-deadline environment Punctuality Attention to detail Posting Salary: $21.82-$28.90 per hour; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Resume Required, Cover Letter Preferred Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application and, for full consideration, please upload a resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.  You are also strongly recommended to upload a cover letter to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.   If you have any questions or difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: Hours: 37.5 hours per week Closing date: Open until filled Note : External job postings will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) ac7e1a3f Last Name (required) 947a96aa Email (required) 153d5155 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Cook San Diego, California Dining Services, Staff The University seeks an individual with a strong interest in working in a mission-driven, faith-based institution. The role of a Cook is working with the campus community and the responsibilities of the position are significantly tethered to the university’s contemporary Roman Catholic mission. Lead Cook - Asian Cuisine San Diego, California Dining Services, Staff The Lead Cook is responsible for aiding in the organization, coordination, and supervision of the preparation of hot food production, maintenance of quality and/or portion control, and the maintenance of sanitation and safety standards. The Lead Cook, under the supervision of the Chef Manager, acts as a working supervisor in training, coordinating, and evaluating the work of the lower-level cooks and other part time staff. Student Life Coordinator San Diego, California Staff, Student Affairs The Student Life Coordinator provides coordination of TRS and other student facing programs and administrative support to the Assistant Vice President for Student Life. Support includes managing calendars, incoming calls, email, and written correspondence as requested. Handles highly confidential information and materials. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f4ccfdef Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Staff Human Resources Staff Employment Type Full-time temporary Full-time temporary Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) cc19d416 Last Name (required) 4e9da0c4 Email (required) abd544ff Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
