    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-biology-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Biology - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Assistant Professor, Biology San Diego, California Faculty Full-time regular 5675 Position Title & Department: Assistant Professor, Biology Posting # 5675 Department Description: The Department of Biology within the College of Arts and Sciences of the University of San Diego, offers a comprehensive program that exposes undergraduate students to concepts across the breadth of biology from the molecular level to ecosystems. In our research-rich curriculum, we emphasize the process of science and the development of skills used in laboratory or field experimental procedures, data analysis and critical reasoning, and communication. Fundamental to our program is a commitment to providing independent research and internship opportunities, which encourage students to work self-sufficiently and assume ownership of their learning as they prepare for graduate and professional schools, teaching in the life sciences, and work in applied biology. Our curriculum also supplements other major studies with a broad background in biology. The College of Arts and Sciences is at the heart of the University of San Diego. Our philosophy is built on the enduring values of the Catholic intellectual tradition, immersing students in the concepts of free inquiry, ethical conduct and compassionate service. The College aims to establish an academic foundation for students to thrive and gain a comprehensive education, which spans the sciences, arts and social sciences. Through our exemplary liberal arts education and rigorous scholarship, we aspire to not only educate the mind but also develop the whole person. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Department of Biology at the University of San Diego invites applications for two tenure-track assistant professorships beginning in Fall 2027 .  The department seeks applicants with experience in cell biology, broadly defined, and/or organismal biology. The successful candidate should demonstrate the potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching and will be expected to teach in majors and non-majors introductory biology courses as well as upper division foundational and/or elective courses according to their area of expertise; the base teaching load is 3 courses (lecture or labs) per semester. A research experience for all students is a central feature of our biology curriculum, and the successful candidate will demonstrate the capacity to develop a robust research program that incorporates undergraduate research students. Job Requirements: Candidates should hold a terminal degree (Ph.D. preferred) in biology or a biology subdiscipline. Candidates should also have demonstrated a commitment to teaching and research, mentoring undergraduates, and fostering a welcoming climate in the classroom and across campus. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Posting Salary: $6,931.25-$7,917 monthly: Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Review of applications will commence on October 16th, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applicants are asked to submit the following materials: Letter of application Curriculum vitae Teaching statement and a sample syllabus. Please discuss your teaching philosophy and approach to inclusive pedagogy. Research statement and a sample of scholarly work. Please include how you will incorporate undergraduates in your research program. Contact information for three references who will be sent a link to upload letters. Contact the Chair of the Department of Biology, Dr. Valerie Hohman ( vhohman@sandiego.edu ) with any questions. For technical difficulties, contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 1ec9d79b Last Name (required) d5951b65 Email (required) 1e265171 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Cook San Diego, California Dining Services, Staff The University seeks an individual with a strong interest in working in a mission-driven, faith-based institution. The role of a Cook is working with the campus community and the responsibilities of the position are significantly tethered to the university’s contemporary Roman Catholic mission. Lead Cook - Asian Cuisine San Diego, California Dining Services, Staff The Lead Cook is responsible for aiding in the organization, coordination, and supervision of the preparation of hot food production, maintenance of quality and/or portion control, and the maintenance of sanitation and safety standards. The Lead Cook, under the supervision of the Chef Manager, acts as a working supervisor in training, coordinating, and evaluating the work of the lower-level cooks and other part time staff. Student Life Coordinator San Diego, California Staff, Student Affairs The Student Life Coordinator provides coordination of TRS and other student facing programs and administrative support to the Assistant Vice President for Student Life. Support includes managing calendars, incoming calls, email, and written correspondence as requested. Handles highly confidential information and materials. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert eeb9cb94 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts and Sciences Faculty College of Arts and Sciences Faculty Employment Type Faculty Full-time regular Faculty Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 669537e1 Last Name (required) e6745d71 Email (required) 5b152ae3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
