    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/acquisitions-and-electronic-resources-assistant-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Acquisitions and Electronic Resources Assistant",
      "description": "Acquisitions and Electronic Resources Assistant - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Acquisitions and Electronic Resources Assistant San Diego, California Full-time regular Closing on: Nov 24 2026 5761 Position Title & Department: Acquisitions and Electronic Resources Assistant; Copley Library Posting # 5761 Department Description: The Helen K. and James S. Copley Library, located on the west end of the campus, currently houses over 500,000 volumes. Collections include books, journals, reference works, databases, government documents, newspapers and electronic journals in many languages, as well as maps, videos, sound recordings, microforms and rare books University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: Reporting to the Senior Electronic and Open Content Librarian in coordination with the Head of Collections, Access, and Discovery, the Acquisitions and Electronic Resources Assistant oversees payment for library materials and assists with the maintenance and assessment of library electronic resources. This position works closely with the Senior Electronic and Open Content Librarian, the Head of Collections, Access, and Discovery, the Budget and Operations Manager, campus Accounts Payable and Procurement departments, and library vendors to ensure timely placement, set up, payment, and receipt of electronic resource orders. This position analyzes, tracks, and manages a variety of data used in the library acquisitions process, including budget and usage data, to support informed acquisition decisions. The role also assists the Senior Electronic and Open Content Librarian with maintaining Copley Library’s electronic resources, such as databases, e-journals, and e-book packages. Additionally, the position coordinates with the Continuing Resources and Licensing Assistant to oversee up to four work-study students. This position works onsite. Duties and Responsibilities: Invoice Processing and Budget Tracking Promptly receives, verifies, and processes library materials invoices and credits in the Integrated Library System (ILS) for timely export to the university accounting system. Performs monthly library acquisition expense reconciliation. Tracks and anticipates invoice renewal schedule for regular library subscriptions. Coordinates with other departments on campus to ensure payment for shared invoices. Maintains order and invoice records for library resources  and communicates with vendors to update records. Works closely with the Senior Electronic and Open Content Librarian to track library resource payment statuses, update payment records, and communicate with the Budget and Operations Manager and Accounts Payable on discrepancies or errors. Provides updates and reports on projected library expenditures as needed to library management. Works with Procurement and library vendors to maintain and update vendor payment profiles in ILS and the university procurement platform. Stays up-to-date with current university, state, and federal tax requirements Usage Data Management and Collections Assessment Harvests and compiles usage data from library vendors and maintains library usage reporting platform. Assists Senior Electronic and Open Content Librarian with analyzing usage, budget, and related library resources data across combined datasets to support informed collection assessment decision-making. Creates and compiles usage reports for internal and external sharing with various groups E-resources Acquisitions and Access Assists Senior Electronic and Open Content Librarian with activation of electronic resource orders, including e-journals, databases, e-book packages, and open access collections. Oversees update notifications in ILS related to electronic collections access. Provides coverage as needed for basic troubleshooting related to technical issues with accessing electronic resources. General and Miscellaneous Duties Coordinates with Continuing Resources and Licensing Assistant to hire, train, supervise, and evaluate up to four work study student assistants. Participates in library activities and committees. Maintains technical knowledge by attending education workshops, etc. Maintains and revises documentation. Other duties as assigned. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. Substitution: A high school diploma plus two years of work experience may substitute for the degree requirement. Strong interest in data reporting required. Preferred Qualifications: Proficiency in Excel and/or Google Sheets (e.g. can understand and apply basic formulas and calculations). Experience with accounts payable processes and practices. Previous academic library experience. Experience with Ex Libris Alma and Workday. Supervisory/leadership experience. Performance Expectations - Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Organizes, prioritizes, and performs detail-oriented tasks. Maintains consistent accuracy and quality during routine work. Writes clearly and concisely for diverse internal and external teams. Excellent, practical computer skills; able to research and find information online. Aptitude and willingness to learn intermediate spreadsheet functions. Works effectively with different teams to problem-solve together. Works independently with guided autonomy. Works with and safeguards confidential information. Demonstrates a commitment to continuous learning and to current trends related to job duties. Enforces and follows Copley Library and University policies. Posting Salary: $21.82-$28.02 Per Hour; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Resume and Cover Letter Required Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application. In addition, please upload a cover letter and resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.  If you have any questions or difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: Hours: 37.5 Hours per week Closing date: November 24 2026 Note : External job postings will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Recommended Jobs Assistant Director of Outreach and Recruitment San Diego, California Administrator, Joan B. Kroc School of Peace Studies The Assistant Director of Outreach and Recruitment plays a key role in advancing the Kroc\nSchool’s strategic enrollment goals across its portfolio of graduate, certificate, and other\nacademic programs. Working collaboratively with the Director of Recruitment and Admissions,\nthe central Enrollment Management team, and other internal and external partners, the\nAssistant Director engages and advises prospective students, supports admissions and\nenrollment activities, coordinates recruitment initiatives and events, and helps admitted students progress toward enrollment. Career Readiness Program Manager San Diego, California Office of Career Services, Staff The Career Readiness Program Manager is responsible for the operational administration, student engagement, and delivery of the Career Readiness Program (CRP - comprising PASSPORT, COMPASS, and CONNECT), a graduation requirement for undergraduate students within the College of Arts and Sciences, the Knauss School of Business, and the Shiley-Marcos School of Engineering. Administrative Director, Consumer Protection Policy Center San Diego, California Administrator, School of Law Under the general direction of the Executive Director of the Centers for Public Interest Law (CPIL) and Consumer Protection Policy Center (CPPC), and reporting to the Children’s Advocacy Institute’s (CAI) Administrative Director, this position is responsible for administrative functions, academic-related functions, and policy-related functions of CPPC. This position coordinates with the directors of CPPC’s two sister organizations at CPIL — CAI and the Energy Policy Initiatives Center (EPIC); CPIL’s Associate Director; and the CPIL/CPPC Executive Director, who oversees all academic instruction of law students enrolled in CPPC courses and clinics. This position also works closely with leadership and colleagues at the USD School of Law and interacts with various offices across the USD campus. Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
